  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-06T22:42:40.616Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, if we were to want a receiver to detect different tags and trigger different animator parameters depending on what is detected, we must duplicate the receiver for each individual tag, which after a certain amount gets ridiculous and presumably unoptimized, especially if you're using multiple receivers to emulate unsupported shapes or longer distances. A simple solution to this could be to add a new Receiver type like \"Collision\" which simply checks to see if the animator offers the tag(s) of the sender.\n\nIf you were to go in depth on this, theoretically you could create multiple options like \"Collision Proximity\", \"Collision Enter\", \"Collision Constant\"",
